---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { EXTERNAL, GOALS, MISSION, SITE, STATS } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema, organizationSchema } from '../lib/schema';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About the ZeroPlastic Movement"
  description="ZeroPlastic is a Sri Lankan environmental movement of 11,000+ volunteers working to cut plastic waste, grow demand for local alternatives and restore the island's coasts and waterways."
  schema={[
    organizationSchema(),
    breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
      { name: 'About', url: '/about/' },
    ]),
  ]}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>Sri Lanka's largest youth-led environmental movement</h1>
      <p class="lede">{MISSION}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="grid grid--stats">
        {
          STATS.map((stat) => (
            <div class="stat">
              <span class="stat__value">{stat.value}</span>
              <span class="stat__label">{stat.label}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>What we have built</h2>
      <p>
        Supported by a network of more than 12,000 change makers, the ZeroPlastic Movement has
        reached over 5 million people with plastic-reduction education, mobilised more than 300,000
        volunteers, and delivered over 1,000 environmental actions and clean-up campaigns.
      </p>
      <p>
        The movement has also empowered and supported over 120 industries focused on plastic
        alternatives and featured over 350 products on its marketplace. Innovative initiatives
        include the creation and deployment of canal and river strainers that stop waste before it
        reaches the ocean, and the ZeroPlastic App, which makes volunteering accessible to young
        people and communities across the island.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our club network spans state universities and campuses nationwide and continues to grow, with
        new ZeroPlastic clubs forming each year. That network is what turns national campaigns into
        local action.
      </p>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        ZeroPlastic works across sectors because plastic pollution cannot be solved by one
        organisation alone. We collaborate with the Central Environmental Authority, our islandwide
        university network, private-sector organisations, development partners, international
        organisations, financial institutions, the travel industry and other institutions working
        to reduce plastic use across Sri Lanka.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our approach combines behaviour change, youth mobilisation, practical plastic alternatives,
        institutional action and policy advocacy. By working through universities, schools,
        communities, businesses and national partners, we aim to create changes that continue
        beyond individual campaigns.
      </p>

      <h2>Helping businesses reduce single-use plastic</h2>
      <p>
        We also work with businesses that want to reduce single-use plastic in their operations.
        Organisations can progress toward recognition through the ZeroPlastic Commitment Standard,
        which carries independent third-party verification by Control Union.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a class="button" href={EXTERNAL.commitment} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">
          Explore the ZeroPlastic Commitment Standard
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Our three goals</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:2rem">
        {
          GOALS.map((goal) => (
            <div>
              <h3>{goal.title}</h3>
              <p style="color:var(--ink-500)">{goal.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:2rem">
        <a class="button" href="/volunteers/">Join {SITE.shortName}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
